        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "chore(tooling): enforce indexed access in core tests",
        "body": "Follow-up to #105343 and #104600.\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe shared test TypeScript config still opted out of `noUncheckedIndexedAccess`, leaving the core test lane's indexed-access assumptions outside the production safety baseline. The July inventory counted 2,685 diagnostics; current `main` had drifted to 2,432.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\n- Removes the final shared test opt-out, so all four test lanes inherit the base `noUncheckedIndexedAccess: true` setting.\n- Burns the core lane from 2,432 diagnostics to zero across 376 test files using iteration where practical, boundary guards where absence is real, and contextual `expectDefined` checks for genuine fixture invariants.\n- Preserves optional-chain spreads, tail lookaheads, first-time paths, and the documented legitimate-absence regression classes.\n- Removes now-redundant explicit `true` settings from the already-landed root, UI, and extension lane configs.\n- Changes test code and test configuration only; no product runtime or dependencies change.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNo runtime impact. Every production and test TypeScript lane now enforces indexed-access safety from the base configuration.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `node scripts/run-tsgo.mjs -p test/tsconfig/tsconfig.core.test.json --incremental false --pretty false` — clean on Blacksmith Testbox; 2,432 diagnostics to zero.\n- `pnpm check:changed` — clean on Blacksmith Testbox in 12m56s, including production/test typechecks, formatting, core/extension/script lint, SDK/package guards, import cycles, and policy checks.\n- `pnpm test:changed` — 33 Vitest shards passed on Blacksmith Testbox in 6m08s, including 2,783 agent tests and all touched core projects.\n- `git diff --check`, targeted oxfmt, and a complete opt-out search — pass; only the base `noUncheckedIndexedAccess: true` remains.\n- Fresh structured autoreview covered all 381 changed files in seven disjoint safety-bounded bundles. No accepted/actionable findings remain; one claimed missing export was rejected with direct barrel-source, strict-compiler, and runtime-test proof.\n\nTestbox lease `tbx_01kxb2j72v773qhzk4dn9aq65c` (`blue-barnacle-626c`).\n",
